From 6c7211ee8b63c24cac7f028d42ae7f7c2a57f6be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:09:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] KDS: reliably show paid app orders, item-based All clearing,
 Square-category routing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1) Paid app order didn't reach the kitchen screen. The hold-until-paid change
   relied on Square clearing the hold flag / returning a payment tender, and both
   can lag — so a genuinely paid order could stay hidden. /api/pay now writes a
   '__paid__' marker in our own DB the instant a payment completes, and the KDS
   treats that (or a tender, or COMPLETED) as 'paid' — a reliable release that
   doesn't depend on Square propagation. releaseHold now flips bc_hold to '0' via
   a metadata value update (preserving bc_store/bc_event) instead of a
   fields_to_clear on a nested key, and the abandoned-order sweep skips anything
   the DB marks paid so it can never bin a paid order.

2) All-orders clearing is item-based (redo of an earlier fix that never
   deployed): an item is handled once ANY station that makes it is bumped, and an
   order leaves All once every item is handled — so a barista bump clears the
   coffee from All even when an overlapping FOH/expo station also lists it.

3) Stations can route by SQUARE category. A live order line carries the item's
   Square category, so the station picker now also offers the real Square
   category names (not just menu/section names). An item Square files under a
   category that isn't one of your menu names (e.g. a Hot Chocolate under 'Hot
   Drinks') now bumps through once that Square category is listed on the station.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
